From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Towfienes <ngolamtien1706@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:56:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] hyprvx: world offsets in render, culling and damage

Patch 0010 of the HyprVX V3 series (Feature 002, T021).

- src/hyprvx/CameraMath.hpp updated to the core header byte for byte
  (transform contract 1.2: offsetCamera, worldDelta; classic include guard).
- src/hyprvx/WindowOffset.{hpp,cpp}: the mechanism API for world offsets
  O(w) (setWindowOffset, windowOffset, contentOffset, resetWindowOffsets;
  contracts/mechanism-api.md 1.0). Storage is private; seams read
  appliedOffset/appliedContentOffset, which are 0 while the window's
  workspace has a fullscreen window (FR-012).
- renderWorkspaceWindows: a window of the active workspace with a world
  offset is drawn under its own hint cameraRenderModif(M,
  offsetCamera(C, O)), then the pass hint returns (research R1). Nothing
  is added for windows without an offset (FR-003).
- visibleOnMonitor, damageWindow and damageSurface use L + O; damageBox's
  union rule also covers boxes at L + O (popup and subsurface map/unmap).
- Pass simplification, direct scanout and solitary client stay off while
  any window has a world offset.
